From 8c2fd22ab29737ef5c7f3275b17157fc3642000f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AyeedShaikh <ayeedxec@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:43:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] toybox: Bind ping -I with the size of the address family on
 FreeBSD

ping -I binds the socket with the size of union socksaddr, 28 bytes.
The FreeBSD kernel sets sa_len from that size, and a raw IPv4 socket
takes only the 16 bytes of struct sockaddr_in, so ping -I failed for
IPv4 with "bind: Invalid argument".  Give the size of the address of
the family, ai_addrlen.

The project freebsd-android-native carries this patch (owner decision
O17).
---
 toys/net/ping.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/toys/net/ping.c b/toys/net/ping.c
index 2833df3..dea3fc4 100644
--- a/toys/net/ping.c
+++ b/toys/net/ping.c
@@ -192,7 +192,12 @@ void ping_main(void)
     }
     xexit();
   }
+#ifdef __FreeBSD__
+  // A FreeBSD raw IPv4 socket takes only the size of an IPv4 address.
+  if (TT.I) xbind(TT.sock, sa, ai->ai_addrlen);
+#else
   if (TT.I) xbind(TT.sock, sa, sizeof(srcaddr));
+#endif
 
 #ifdef __FreeBSD__
   // The ttl is in the IP header of each reply. The socket cookie tags the
